[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Software Requirements Specification - Operating Scenarios
UID: DOC-SSS003
VERSION: 1.1.0
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Text

[[SECTION]]
UID: SEC-SSS3-COVER
TITLE: Scenario suite coverage

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Operating scenarios exercise the patented iron-air plant. Charge, discharge, and
LODES durations follow US12308414B2 (8 h to seasonal, including about 100 h and
300 h). Chemistry faults follow EP4602674A1 HER competition, magnetite conversion,
and thick-electrode transport. Air and mechanical faults follow US12308414B2
flooding, dry-out, sparging, fan/pump, and containment disclosures. Software
scenario results are not hardware validation of either patent.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Charge scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required charge scenarios: constant-current, constant-power, constant-voltage,
charge tapering, partial charge, charge termination, overcharge protection,
low-temperature charging, high-temperature charging, charging with hydrogen
evolution, and charging with limited electrolyte circulation.

Charge current greater than 6 mA/g to at least twice rated capacity SHALL be an
allowed formation/full-charge protocol (EP4602674A1 [0261]). Dual-electrode charge
SHALL use the OER path (EP4602674A1 [0049]).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 rechargeable metal-air operation; EP4602674A1 charge through OER and
HER competition on thick iron electrodes.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Changed because ironair.scenarios is empty and not every IA-SCN-CHG-* ID has a
notebook. Executable charge coverage is plant_sim/91_ChargeDischarge.ipynb and
plant_sim.scenarios.mission.charge_discharge_inputs. Remaining CHG IDs are design
allocations until dedicated notebooks exist.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Discharge scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required discharge scenarios: constant-current, constant-power, variable-load,
partial discharge, deep discharge, oxygen-limited, thermal-limited, high-rate,
low-rate, and 100-hour discharge.

Discharge SHALL use the ORR path (EP4602674A1 [0049]). 100 h and 300 h discharges
SHALL be available, corresponding to about 3-5 cm and 4-6 cm anode thickness in
US12308414B2. Oxygen-limited discharge SHALL include restricted pO2 within
0.01-100 atm (US12308414B2).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 duration versus anode thickness; EP4602674A1 dual-electrode discharge
to Fe(OH)2 / Fe3O4.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Changed because ironair.scenarios is empty. Executable discharge coverage is
plant_sim/91_ChargeDischarge.ipynb (including 100 h duration) and
charge_discharge_inputs. Remaining DCH IDs are design allocations.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Transition scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required transition scenarios: charge to discharge, discharge to charge, rapid power
reversal, rest period, voltage relaxation, repeated cycling, startup, shutdown, and
restart after protection trip.

Charge/discharge transitions SHALL operate the EP4602674A1 [0049] / US12308414B2
FIGS. 5A-5B electrode switch, including electrical isolation of ORR during OER
to protect the air electrode.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Changed because ironair.scenarios is empty. Executable transition coverage is
plant_sim/90_Commissioning.ipynb plus charge/discharge mode switches in
91_ChargeDischarge.ipynb. Remaining TRN IDs are design allocations.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Chemistry scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required chemistry scenarios: iron passivation, magnetite formation, hydrogen evolution,
oxygen starvation, carbonate accumulation, water depletion, electrolyte dilution,
electrolyte concentration increase, electrode aging, and catalyst degradation.

Chemistry scenarios SHALL include planar versus channeled versus interdigitated
coulombic-efficiency comparison at 6 M KOH and 303 K (EP4602674A1 FIGS. 19-27)
and carbonate clogging of air-electrode pores (US12308414B2).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Changed because ironair.scenarios is empty. Executable chemistry-fault coverage is
plant_sim/95_CarbonationAndImpurity.ipynb and 98_DegradationCE.ipynb.
Remaining CHM IDs are design allocations.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Environmental scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required environmental scenarios: cold start, hot start, ambient temperature cycling,
high relative humidity, low relative humidity, high altitude, reduced atmospheric
oxygen, and thermal control failure.

Environmental cases SHALL include US12308414B2 25 C / 1 atm reference, EP4602674A1
303 K KOH reference, high-humidity flooding of GDE, low-humidity dry-out, and
reduced pO2.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Changed because ironair.scenarios is empty. Executable environmental coverage is
plant_sim/93_ThermalExcursion.ipynb. Remaining ENV IDs are design allocations.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Mechanical fault scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required mechanical fault scenarios: fan failure, pump failure, filter blockage,
valve failure, electrolyte leak, reservoir depletion, reduced circulation, heat
exchanger failure, and ventilation failure.

Mechanical faults SHALL include loss of sparge/air supply to submerged ORR, ORR
flooding versus dry-out, lid-vent blockage, and primary-vessel leak into secondary
containment (US12308414B2 vessel cavity 161).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Changed because ironair.scenarios is empty. Executable mechanical-fault coverage is
plant_sim/94_StarvationAndFlooding.ipynb. Remaining MCH IDs are design allocations.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Electrical scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required electrical scenarios: cell short, cell open circuit, cell imbalance, stack
mismatch, converter overload, DC bus undervoltage, DC bus overvoltage, inverter
current limit, and sensor failure.

Electrical scenarios SHALL include can-negative housing contact faults, ORR/OER
toggle-switch stuck states, and stacked-vessel series-contact opens
(US12308414B2 Claims 3, 5, 16).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Changed because ironair.scenarios is empty. Electrical BOP ODEs are demonstrated in
plant_sim/33_ElectricalBalance.ipynb. Dedicated ELC fault notebooks remain design
allocations.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Grid scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required grid scenarios: voltage sag, voltage swell, underfrequency, overfrequency,
frequency-watt response, volt-var response, grid disconnection, reconnection,
ride-through, and active/reactive power limits.

Grid scenarios SHALL cover LODES services from milliseconds to seasonal windows
as framed in US12308414B2 Background and FIGS. 94-102.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Changed because ironair.scenarios is empty. Executable grid coverage is
plant_sim/92_GridServices.ipynb. Remaining GRD IDs are design allocations.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Long-term scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required long-term scenarios: 100-hour discharge, multiple-day energy dispatch,
charge/discharge cycling, seasonal storage, calendar aging, cycle aging, capacity
fade, efficiency degradation, and annual operating profile.

Long-term scenarios SHALL include 100 h and 300 h discharges, summer-to-winter
seasonal storage of surplus solar, and calendar aging of replaceable electrodes
(US12308414B2 Definitions and replaceable-electrode discussion).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Each listed scenario has a unique IA-SCN-LT-* ID, Python scenario function, and notebook.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Characterization scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required characterization scenarios: current-voltage polarization curves,
charge/discharge voltage versus SOC, efficiency versus power, efficiency versus
temperature, SOC versus time, oxygen demand versus power, hydrogen generation versus
charge current, KOH concentration sweep, thermal response, parameter sensitivity,
and uncertainty analysis.

Characterization SHALL include planar versus interdigitated discharge voltage
versus capacity (EP4602674A1 FIG. 27), coulombic efficiency versus charge time
(FIGS. 19, 21, 23, 25), and area-specific resistance versus time (FIGS. 20, 22,
24, 26) at documented 6 M KOH and 303 K.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Each listed scenario has a unique IA-SCN-CHR-* ID, Python scenario function, and notebook.
<<<

