[[SECTION]]
UID: SEC-SSS3-PAT
TITLE: Patent-architecture scenarios

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
These scenarios map US12308414B2 Claims 1-18 and EP4602674A1 Claims 1, 20, 38, 55,
70, 77, and FIGS. 19-27 onto executable ironair scenario functions.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-PAT-STACKORR
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Submerged stacked ORR equal pressure drop
STATEMENT: >>>
Operate a vertical stack of discrete submerged ORR sections with depth-dependent
geometry and equal pressure drop in the depth direction (US12308414B2 Claim 1).
Record air utilization, pO2, and ORR current versus height.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Pressure drop across each stacked section is the same. Bubble cascade reaches
upper sections. No external electrolyte leak is required for internal flooding.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-PAT-DRI
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DRI pellet bed anode
STATEMENT: >>>
Discharge and charge a packed bed of direct reduced iron pellets
(US12308414B2 Claim 18; FIG. 3) in 6 M KOH.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Iron inventory oxidizes to Fe(OH)2 / Fe3O4 on discharge. Pellet-bed porosity
absorbs discharge volume increase (EP4602674A1 [0043]).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-PAT-INTERDIG
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Interdigitated OER versus planar control
STATEMENT: >>>
Compare planar iron/OER, channeled iron with planar OER, and channeled iron with
interdigitated OER at 6 M KOH, 303 K, initial rib porosity 0.6, ChanFrac 0.4,
w_rib 5 mm, and 4 g Fe/cm2 (EP4602674A1 FIGS. 19-27).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Interdigitated configuration shows higher coulombic efficiency and an extended
upper discharge voltage plateau relative to planar, matching FIG. 27 qualitative
behavior. Software comparison is verification against the disclosed trends, not
reproduction of unpublished experimental tables.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-CHM-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-PAT-ASYM
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Asymmetric 100 h charge and 300 h discharge
STATEMENT: >>>
Configure independent charge and discharge length scales for about 100 h charge
and about 300 h discharge with a 5 cm by 5 cm anode cross-section
(US12308414B2 asymmetric-duration example).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Charge duration and discharge duration are independently tunable. SOC and Faraday
accounting remain consistent over both windows.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-PAT-FLOAT
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Floating ORR with submerged OER
STATEMENT: >>>
Float the ORR at the electrolyte free surface while the OER remains submerged
(US12308414B2 Summary; FIGS. 1B-3). Vary electrolyte height by evaporation and
confirm the ORR remains at the triple-phase boundary.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
ORR follows the free surface. OER remains wetted. Flooding and dry-out flags stay
clear under slow height change.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-PAT-SPIRAL
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Spiral bifilar iron and OER
STATEMENT: >>>
Assemble spiral iron and anode current collector with spiral OER at least
partially bifilar and ORR facing the spiral axis (EP4602674A1 Claim 70).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Iron and OER remain interdigitated along the spiral. ORR air face is toward the
axis of rotation. Electrolyte contacts iron, ORR first surface, and OER.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-PAT-PLEAT
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Pleated iron and OER
STATEMENT: >>>
Operate pleated iron and pleated OER with channels between pleats
(EP4602674A1 Claim 77; FIG. 17), optionally with OER on both iron faces
(Claim 80).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Channels exist between pleats. OER occupies channels perpendicular to the ORR
plane. Dual-face OER is a selectable option.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-PAT-PO2
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Adjustable oxygen partial pressure
STATEMENT: >>>
Raise pO2 on discharge within 0.01-100 atm and lower pO2 on charge within
0.001-100 atm (US12308414B2 pressurized-gas paragraph).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Discharge driving force increases with pO2. Charge OER is not forced to high pO2.
Solver remains within property-model domain.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-022

[[/SECTION]]
